Z||000005||Greg Piet||10-07-1999||10:36 AM||||The convertable with the top down looks really good!  How does it look with the top up?<BR>Also for anyone who has done this, what happens to the dome light assy (namely the amazing "Performance Sound" slider).<p>[This message has been edited by Greg Piet (edited 10-07-1999).]||||reg||1
Z||000006||MIKLAV||10-07-1999||12:44 PM||||I dated a girl who had a '87 Blue coupe convertable w/black top pull over style.  It look great with the top down.  To bad she didn't have wing on it or ground effects, that would have been sweet!  The brake light had to be removed and placed on top of engine compartment. No interior lights only ones where down by the feet. The car did have lots of water leaks. She won the car at some radio station contest, so I don't know who did the conversion.  The windshield would move, it need more support.  Heating the interior was a problem during the winter time<BR>The gas cap release lever had to be relocated. Overall the car was fun.<BR>Mike<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000007||RZURCTN||10-07-1999||02:08 PM||||What supports the windshield when you convert to a convertable?  If you hit 110mph will the windshiled cave in?  My previuous 84 had a problem with the roof comming away from the windshield.  I guess that the AZ sun was getting to it somewhat.||||reg||5
